The Result: Instead of bouncing back when hitting an impurity, the electron simply flows right around it like water around a pebble and continues forward.
Significance for Computers: Data (represented by electron streams or spin alignments) never suffers from random bit-flips caused by scattering during transmission. This achieves lossless, high-fidelity information transfer, fundamentally eliminating data loss due to device heating and signal decay.
